know that through your prayers and the provision of the Spirit of Jesus Christ, my distress will turn out for my deliverance.","from":12},{"book":"JAS","chapter":5,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Therefore confess your sins to each other and pray for each other so that you may be healed. The prayer of a righteous man has great power to prevail.","from":11},{"book":"PSA","chapter":56,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Then my enemies will retreat on the day I cry for help. By this I will know that God is on my side.","from":11},{"book":"HEB","chapter":12,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Therefore strengthen your limp hands and weak knees.","from":12},{"book":"MRK","chapter":14,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Then Jesus returned and found them sleeping. “Simon, are you asleep?” He asked. “Were you not able to keep watch for one hour?","from":12},{"book":"MRK","chapter":14,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"And again Jesus returned and found them sleeping, for their eyes were heavy. And they did not know what to answer Him.","from":12}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":4}]},"14-16":{"people":[{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":2,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"places":[{"id":"amalek-h6002g","name":"Amalek","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":2,"firstVerse":14}],"words":[{"base":"H4229","lemma":"מָחָה","tr":"ma·chah","gloss":"to wipe","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":36},{"base":"H6002","lemma":"עֲמָלֵק","tr":"a·ma·leq","gloss":"Amalek","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":39},{"base":"H1755","lemma":"דּוֹר","tr":"dor","gloss":"generation","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":167},{"base":"H4872","lemma":"מֹשֶׁה","tr":"mo·sheh","gloss":"Moses","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":766},{"base":"H5251","lemma":"נֵס","tr":"nes","gloss":"Banner","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":21},{"base":"H2143","lemma":"זֵ֫כֶר","tr":"ze·kher","gloss":"memorial","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":23},{"base":"H2146","lemma":"זִכָּרוֹן","tr":"zikh·ron","gloss":"memorial","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H3050","lemma":"יָהּ","tr":"yah","gloss":"LORD","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":48},{"base":"H5612","lemma":"סֵ֫פֶר","tr":"se·pher","gloss":"scroll: document","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":186},{"base":"H0241","lemma":"אֹ֫זֶן","tr":"o·zen","gloss":"ear","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":187}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":22,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":32,"source":"both","text":"And Abraham called that place The LordWill Provide. So to this day it is said, “On the mountain of the Lordit will be provided.”","from":15},{"book":"JDG","chapter":6,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"So Gideon built an altar to the LORD there and called it The LORD Is Peace. To this day it stands in Ophrah of the Abiezrites.","from":15},{"book":"EXO","chapter":34,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The LORD also said to Moses, “Write down these words, for in accordance with these words I have made a covenant with you and with Israel.”","from":14},{"book":"PSA","chapter":60,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"You have raised a banner for those who fear You, that they may flee the bow. Selah","from":15},{"book":"GEN","chapter":33,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"There he set up an altar and called it El-Elohe-Israel.","from":15},{"book":"EXO","chapter":12,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And this day will be a memorial for you, and you are to celebrate it as a feast to the LORD, as a permanent statute for the generations to come.","from":14},{"book":"EXO","chapter":13,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"It shall be a sign for you on your hand and a reminder on your forehead that the Law of the LORD is to be on your lips. For with a mighty hand the LORD brought you out of Egypt.","from":14},{"book":"NUM","chapter":24,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Balaam saw Amalek and lifted up an oracle, saying: “Amalek was first among the nations, but his end is destruction.”","from":14}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":2}]}}